  "preamble": "The alveolar nasal [n] becomes bilabial [m] by regressive place assimilation to a following labial consonant. Synchronically it is regular in Spanish and Modern Greek (also across word boundaries), and historically it has fixed [m] in words such as English hemp and Turkish ambar.",
  "phoneticEffects": "Place Assimilation, Regressive Assimilation",
